\section{Description of the main subroutines}
\label{sec04}
\setcounter{equation}{0}
\setcounter{figure}{0}
The SIMTET package constitutes two main subroutines SIM0ONEI and SIM0TWOI. 
Similar subroutines are provided for the one-dimensional and two-dimensional integrals.
These subroutines, which are  to be called from the main program, have the following 
structure: %
\begin{itemize}
%
\item  SUBROUTINE SIM0ONEI(SIM0, SIM0I, VERM) .\\
       SIM0ONEI computes the integrals $r_0$ and  $s_0$ which  
       are given by (\ref{equ:2.17}) and  (\ref{equ:2.21}), respectively. \\
\begin{tabular}{rl}
 {\it input}: VERM(4) = & four complex numbers $(z_i,i=1,...,4)$ for the \\ 
              &         values of the denominator function at each of four \\
              &         tetrahedron corners, as shown in Figure~\ref{fig:2.1}. \\
 {\it output}: \ \ \ \ SIM0 = &   complex number for the value of integral $r_0$. \\
              SIM0I = &   complex number for the value of integral $s_0$. \\
\end{tabular}
 At the start, the input complex numbers in VERM(4) are sent to  
 SIM0LEPS, where the proper case a), b), c) or d) is 
 selected and subroutine SIM1ONEI,  SIM2ONEI, 
 SIM3ONEI or  SIM4ONEI is called, respectively. 
%
\item SUBROUTINE SIM0TWOI(VERL, VERLI, VERM). \\
       SIM0TWOI computes the integrals $r_i$ and $s_i$ (i=1,..,4), given by
       (\ref{equ:2.27}) and (\ref{equ:2.29}), respectively. \\
\begin{tabular}{rl}
 {\it input}:  VERM(4) = & four complex numbers as in SIM0ONEI . \\
 {\it output}: VERL(4) = & four complex values of 
                           integrals $r_i (i=1,...,4)$. \\
              VERLI(4) = & four complex values of 
                           integrals $s_i (i=1,...,4)$. \\
\end{tabular}
 Similarly, as in the case of SIM0ONEI, the four 
 complex numbers in VERM(4) are first sent to SIM0LEPS, where the proper
 case a), b), c) or d) is selected, and subroutine 
 SIM1TWOI,  SIM2TWOI, SIM3TWOI or  SIM4TWOI is called, respectively. \\
% 
 The auxiliary subroutines have the following structure:\\
\item SUBROUTINE SIM0LEPS(VERM, N, W, AS, LONE, EPS, LEPS) \\
\begin{tabular}{r l}
 {\it input}: VERM(4) = & four complex numbers as in SIM0ONEI . \\
 {\it output}: \ \ \ \ \ W(3) = & three complex $w$-numbers resulting from the \\
                         & transformation defined in (\ref{equ:3.2}) with \\
                         & the number N=1,..,4. \\
                 AS(3) = & real array with the three values associated with \\
                         & the imaginary term in (\ref{equ:3.8}). If any \\ 
                         &  $w_i$-argument falls out of the unit circle, \\ 
                         & it must be reflected back to its interior. \\
%                EPSONE = & critical distance $|w2-ONE|$ or $|w2+ONE|$ \\
               LONE(4) = & logical array storing the information regarding which case, \\
                         & as described in Section \ref{sec03}, must be chosen. \\
                   EPS = &  critical distance $|w1-w2|$ etc. \\
               LEPS(3) = & logical array keeping the information, of how close \\
                         & the three $w_i$-numbers are to each other on \\ 
                         & the complex plane. Control of the selection between \\ 
                         & the three degenerated cases is kept by setting \\ 
                         & value of real variable EPS.
\end{tabular}
\item  SUBROUTINE S1D0ONEI(SIM0, SIM0I, VERM) .\\
       S1D0ONEI computes the one-dimensional integral $r^{(1)}_0$ in (\ref{equ:2.7}) 
       and its $z$-integral. 
%
\item SUBROUTINE S1D0TWOI(VERL, VERLI, VERM). \\
       S1D0TWOI computes the one-dimensional partial integrals $r^{(1)}_i$ 
       and their $z$-integrals. 
%
\item  SUBROUTINE S2D0ONEI(SIM0, SIM0I, VERM) .\\
       S2D0ONEI computes the two-dimensional integral $r^{(2)}_0$ in (\ref{equ:2.11}) 
       and its $z$-integral. 
%
\item SUBROUTINE S2D0TWOI(VERL, VERLI, VERM). \\
       S2D0TWOI computes the two-dimensional partial integrals $r^{(2)}_i$ 
       and their $z$-integrals. 
%
\end{itemize}


